**This section supersedes the Wave 6 pointer below.** Owner instructed the
orchestrator to run Wave 7 autonomously through A10, with no shell/edit
permission prompts for any role. Baseline is clean synchronized `d38db82`;
Wave 6 is concluded. The active driver is `wave7`, policy
`judgment=autonomous`, `judge_budget=500`, and no process is currently running
after the A4 gate halt.

Scope: **214 unique items / 179 proof-bearing / 12 pages / 6 A/B pairs**, split
into four legal Beta batches: real-analysis completeness/limits (64),
real-analysis series (37), topology separation/Urysohn (52), and topology
uniform spaces (61). A0 and A2 are complete and gated. The relationship
manifest has 1,810 edges (1,296 published-backward, 492 same-batch, 12
cross-batch, 10 forward). Four Sol Betas completed all 214 provenance rows and
all 179 proof contracts. A3 completed at `wave7-A3.md`; all four A4 apply lanes
completed and changed 194 item/page files.

The driver then halted correctly at A4: 11/13 gates pass. Exact blockers:

- `proof-contract`: four errors — an ineligible generated Laurent-series
  counterexample cited by `ex-cauchy-complete-not-complete-field`; unused L8 in
  `ex-harmonic-series-diverges`; and generated direct corollary
  `cor-complete-normality-is-hereditary` cited by
  `cor-perfect-normality-is-hereditary`.
- `content-policy`: 23 `established-knowledge` rows remain untagged pending
  Alpha concurrence, plus the generated-target containment findings.

Root cause: A3 repeated the historical over-broad reading that removing an
invalid dependency edge, unused Fact, or unsupported ancillary claim is an
owner-only “deletion”. The durable Wave 3 precedent in this file already says
owner-only deletion means item/id removal or structural reading-order change;
ordinary citation/dependency/claim repairs remain delegated under R1. A3 also
treated source-backed repair clauses as owner-only although
`AUDIT-WORKFLOW.md` says only deletions, id changes, and structural reading
order are held.

**Exact next actions:** (1) append an orchestrator correction to `wave7-A3.md`
authorizing the already-verified delegated repairs and generated-target
containment; (2) dispatch one narrow Sol Alpha recovery lane to adjudicate the
23 D2 concurrences from disk and amend the ledger rows, without repeating A6;
(3) re-dispatch only the affected A4 Betas to apply the corrected decisions,
